WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.067
"Three Reasons Fruits and Vegetables
May Reduce Osteoporosis Risk"

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.240
Even just
a single extra serving

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.400
of fruits
and vegetables per day

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.760
is associated
with lower bone fracture risk.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.920
Why?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.560
Well, osteoporotic fracture risk

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.080
is associated
with higher levels

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.440
of inflammation
in your blood,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.000
for example,
C-reactive protein,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.080
and specifically,
a more pro-inflammatory diet.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.960
Those eating higher on
the dietary inflammatory index

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.520
have about a 30 percent
greater risk

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.160
of osteoporosis
and fracture

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.880
than those eating
more anti-inflammatory diets,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.760
and a higher intake
of fruits and vegetables

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.320
decreases inflammation.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.880
So, that's one possible reason.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.760
Free radicals
may also play a role

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.320
in eating away at your bone,

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.040
suggesting that pro-oxidant
stress may contribute

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.640
to osteoporosis.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.200
Both the total antioxidant power

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.480
and capacity of people's
bloodstreams and diets

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.960
are significantly lower
in those with osteoporosis,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.920
and how do we squash
free radicals

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.760
and improve antioxidant status?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.560
With fruits and vegetables.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.800
For example, consumption
of vitamin C-rich foods

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.720
is associated with lower risk
of hip fracture, osteoporosis,

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.960
and bone loss.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.640
Every additional increase of
50mg of dietary vitamin C a day,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.040
which is about
the equivalent of one orange,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.560
may lower the risk of hip
fracture by 5 percent.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.600
The third way fruits and
vegetables may help our bones

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.600
is through acid-base balance.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.480
As we grow older,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.640
there's a slight drop
in the pH of our blood,

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.520
as our blood becomes
more acidic with age.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.760
This is thought to be due to the
waning ability of our kidneys

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.080
to excrete excess acid.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.760
In vitro studies suggest a drop
in pH may lead to activation

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.400
of the cells
that break down bone

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.680
and an inhibition of cells
that build bone back up.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.040
So, how about eating
alkaline-forming foods?

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.360
The most acid-forming foods
are meat and cheese,

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.320
especially fish,

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.480
and the most alkaline,
or base-forming, foods

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.040
are fruits and vegetables.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.160
This may help explain why

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.600
if you experimentally
remove fruits and vegetables

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.460
from people's diets,

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.280
a marker of bone formation
significantly drops,

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.600
and a marker of bone loss
shoots up,

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.080
and vice-versa when you
add fruits and vegetables

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.800
back into their daily diets.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.280
The greater the estimated ratio

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.560
between acid-forming foods
and alkaline-forming foods,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.600
the greater the risk
of hip fracture,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.440
supporting the rationale
to eat less acidic diets,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.760
but this was based
on observational data.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.440
To prove cause-and-effect,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.440
two-year, double-blind,
randomized controlled trials

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.840
were performed in which

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.680
the three added servings
of fruits and vegetables,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.880
or the equivalent
of six extra servings,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.480
failed to have an effect.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.560
But randomize people
to the equivalent

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.880
of nine daily servings
of fruits' and vegetables' worth

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.680
of an alkaline-forming compound

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.600
and you do see
a significant increase

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.520
in bone volume and density
in the spine, hip,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.760
and throughout the whole body.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.120
Are there any
fruits and vegetables

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.440
that are particularly good?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:59.760
That's the question
I'll address next.

